  "concept": "The Carnot cycle is a sequence of four reversible processes — isothermal expansion, adiabatic expansion, isothermal compression, adiabatic compression — in which heat crosses the system boundary only during the two isothermal steps while the gas is in contact with a reservoir, while the insulated adiabatic steps shuttle the gas between the two reservoir temperatures.",
  "figureType": "diagram",
